Kylin NGCC Implementation Package

This package contains first-stage NGCC digital-signature implementations for:

- Kylin-128
- Kylin-256
- Kylin-512

The reference implementation is portable C99. The optimized implementation
currently uses the same portable source code with an `-O3 -march=native` build
profile for mainstream 64-bit PC processors; deeper code-level optimization is
tracked as later work.

The packaged NGCC wrappers accept messages up to `2^60` bytes, i.e. `2^63`
bits, matching the submission bound recorded in the draft.

Run the full repository-local verification flow from the repository root:

    make verify

This refreshes parameter output, rebuilds all six instances, runs the
self-tests, regenerates the reference KAT files, and updates the package-level
benchmark and memory summaries.

Build all instances only:

    for d in Implementations/Reference_Implementation/Kylin-* \
             Implementations/Optimized_Implementation/Kylin-*; do
        (cd "$d" && make clean && make && make test)
    done

Generate reference KAT vectors:

    for d in Implementations/Reference_Implementation/Kylin-*; do
        (cd "$d" && make kat)
    done

Generated KAT files are stored in `Test_Vectors/`.

Refresh the package-level benchmark and memory summaries only:

    make metrics

This updates:

- `paper/data/package_bench.csv`
- `paper/data/package_memory.csv`
- `Implementations/benchmarks/summary.md`
